(TYP-01 Discrepancy 1, companion: the same `number` variable holding a
 WHOLE value classifies the opposite way under `is a` — proves the
 predicate's tag tracks the runtime value's shape, not the variable's
 static declared type, since TYP-01.vox's `n` (declared identically,
 `a number called n`) flips both answers when its value is whole.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D1-frac.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   is a number: yes
   is a decimal: no
)
a number called n is 3.
if n is a number, print "is a number: yes". otherwise print "is a number: no".
if n is a decimal, print "is a decimal: yes". otherwise print "is a decimal: no".
